# Letrec type inference: sibling TypeVar must resolve to concrete type.
# Before the fix, b's type would remain TypeVar rather than resolving to Int.
# Sibling b references sibling a: [length a] where a: "hello" must produce Int(5).
# The absence of === warn asserts that no spurious type warnings are emitted.
[a: "hello"  b: [length a]]
=== out
Dict({"a": String("hello"), "b": Int(5)})
---
# Forward-reference pattern: b references a, but a is defined AFTER b in the dict.
# Letrec scope means all keys are visible to all values regardless of order.
# The absence of === warn asserts that no spurious type warnings are emitted.
[b: [length a]  a: "hello"]
=== out
Dict({"a": String("hello"), "b": Int(5)})
